# Type seeds for Spinel (spinel --rbs sig), passed by sim_spinel/build.sh.
#
# Spinel 2026.09.12 infers the filter's two integrator states as untyped, which turns soft_clip,
# flush_tiny, clip_output and process into boxed arithmetic on every sample (and makes the C
# compile take tens of minutes). Declared Float, they compile as before. A seed is trusted, not
# checked, so this has to stay true: both states only ever hold a Float.
module Spms1
  class Filter
    @s1: Float
    @s2: Float
  end
end
